# cp(1)

## NAME

cp - copy files and directories

## SYNOPSIS

    cp [-rR] source dest
    cp [-rR] source... directory

## DESCRIPTION

Copies files. If the destination is a directory, each source is copied into it under the same name. A directory is never copied into itself. Symbolic links inside a copied tree are not copied.

## OPTIONS

- `-r, -R`: copy directories and their contents
- `-f`: accepted and ignored

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand
- `2`: usage error

## SEE ALSO

mv(1), rm(1)
